-- title:
--   Poisson random measure: finite families of marked disjoint time-strip integrals are independent
-- statement:
--   For every monotone finite grid on nonnegative time, the real-valued marked Poisson integrals on successive disjoint half-open strips are jointly independent as an iIndepFun family. Prove by the structural PoissonRandomMeasure.independent_disjoint count law together with measurability of the marked integral with respect to the σ-algebra generated by evaluations of N on measurable subsets of its own strip. Finite intensity guarantees almost-sure finite atomic support. This is a genuinely nontrivial joint independence theorem, stronger than independence of two counts.
-- source:
--   Kyprianou (2006), Eq. (2.3), independent-increments branch, actual LevyStochCalc PoissonRandomMeasure with independent_disjoint and measurable_eval fields; mission ed6e9edb-945b-4dc1-bb4b-3eed54f89dd0.

import Mathlib
import Definitions.Def_KLSModular_LevyStochCalc_Poisson_RandomMeasure
import Definitions.Def_LeanLevy_Processes_LevyProcess
open MeasureTheory ProbabilityTheory
open scoped ENNReal NNReal
set_option autoImplicit false

theorem Kyprianou.Ch02.prmFiniteRegionDisjointMarkedStripIntegralsIndependentV1
    {Ω : Type} [MeasurableSpace Ω] (P : Measure Ω)
    [IsProbabilityMeasure P] (ν : Measure ℝ) [SigmaFinite ν]
    (N : LevyStochCalc.Poisson.PoissonRandomMeasure.{0, 0, 0} P ν)
    (B : Set ℝ) (hB : MeasurableSet B)
    (hfinite : ν B < ⊤) :
    ∀ (n : ℕ) (t : Fin (n + 1) → ℝ≥0) (ht : Monotone t),
      iIndepFun (fun (i : Fin n) (ω : Ω) =>
        ∫ z in (Set.Ioc (t i.castSucc : ℝ) (t i.succ : ℝ) ×ˢ B),
          z.2 ∂(N.N ω)) P := by sorry
